(The BRC February 2026 Crime Survey confirms what investigators have known for years: a significant share of) Tj
T* (retail theft is not impulsive. It is organised. Groups select stores the way a buyer selects a supplier, using) Tj
T* (product density, staff-to-floor ratios, camera blind spots, and proximity to resale infrastructure as selection) Tj
T* (criteria.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.353 0.275 0.157 rg
0. Tc
62.3622047244094517 584.5041732283464171 Td
(The conventional response to this problem has not changed in forty years. Cameras, guards, EAS tags, ink dye) Tj
T* (packs. All of these are deterrents aimed at the act of theft. None of them address the underlying economics that) Tj
T* (make retail theft a viable business model.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.353 0.275 0.157 rg
0. Tc
62.3622047244094517 527.2443307086613231 Td
(The theft is not the business. The resale is. A stolen razor from a Salford Boots that cannot be sold on Vinted is) Tj
T* (worthless to the OCG that took it. The security industry has spent forty years trying to stop the acquisition) Tj
T* (phase. It has not spent nearly enough time poisoning the liquidation phase.) Tj
